libfprint-goodix-spi (0.0~git20261019.505dc7e-1+forky1) forky; urgency=medium

  * Target Debian 14 "forky" instead of trixie.
  * Rebuilt in a forky environment. The only change in the generated
    dependency set is the gusb runtime package, which forky renamed
    libgusb2 -> libgusb2a while keeping the SONAME (libgusb.so.2). All other
    Depends entries are identical to the trixie build, and the binary payload
    is unchanged.
  * The +forky1 suffix keeps this build distinguishable from a trixie build,
    which carries the same upstream version but a dependency name that cannot
    be satisfied on forky (dpkg-shlibdeps derives package names from the build
    host, not from the target suite).
  * README.Debian: build instructions retargeted to forky; new subsection on
    "No devices available", i.e. how to tell "firmware does not expose the
    sensor" from "the package is broken" (ACPI _STA returning 0).

 -- libfprint-goodix-spi packagers <packagers@example.invalid>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 02:40:00 +0800

libfprint-goodix-spi (0.0~git20261019.505dc7e-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging of the out-of-tree Goodix GDIX51C0 SPI driver
    for libfprint.
  * Build system mirrors upstream install.sh, but runs at package build time:
    pinned libfprint v1.94.10 and fprintd v1.94.5 are fetched with the
    project's own scripts, patched with patches/libfprint/ and patches/fprintd/
    and compiled locally.
  * Installation mirrors upstream install.sh as well: the patched libfprint
    and the patched fprintd are installed as a private shadow pair below
    /opt/goodix-spi-driver. Nothing is placed in the system library
    directories, and the shadow libfprint is not registered with ldconfig or
    with a shlibs/symbols entry, so it cannot be picked up accidentally by
    binaries other than fprintd.service.
  * fprintd.service is redirected to the shadow pair through systemd drop-ins
    in /etc/systemd/system/fprintd.service.d (LD_LIBRARY_PATH, ExecStart
    replacement, GDIX51C0 warm-session opt-in).
  * The udev rule generated by the patched libfprint is installed as
    /etc/udev/rules.d/70-libfprint-2.rules, with the GDIX51C0 ACPI modalias
    match widened to a glob so firmware that also advertises a _CID still
    binds spidev.
  * Sensor key, calibration and enrolled prints are left in /var/lib/fprint
    and are not removed on purge; the cleanup paths are documented in
    README.Debian.

 -- libfprint-goodix-spi packagers <packagers@example.invalid>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
